## Vercel Speed Insights Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project.

### What was implemented:

1. **Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` (version ^1.3.1) using pnpm
   - Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with the new dependency

2. **Component Integration**
   - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
   - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the root layout (app/layout.tsx)
   - Placed the component inside the `<body>` tag, after the `<Analytics />` component

### Files Modified:
- `mudra-app/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `mudra-app/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated lock file with new dependency
- `mudra-app/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

### Implementation Details:

The project uses Next.js 16.1.3 with the App Router, so the import from `@vercel/speed-insights/next` was used (recommended for Next.js 13.5+). The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout to ensure it's available across all pages.

The component is placed after the existing `<Analytics />` component from Vercel Analytics, maintaining consistency with other tracking and monitoring integrations already present in the application.

### Verification:

- Package was successfully installed and appears in package.json and lock file
- The `/next` export path exists in the @vercel/speed-insights package
- The layout file structure is preserved and maintains all existing functionality
- The component is correctly positioned within the body tag alongside other UI providers

The integration is now complete and ready to collect Web Vitals data from the application.
